### Stockly API test script (IntelliJ HTTP Client). Save in backend/docs/ and open in IntelliJ.
### Run the requests TOP TO BOTTOM, using the green arrow beside each "###" line. Expected result is written above each request.
### Assumes a FRESH database (no sample data), so the first category, product and order get id 1.
### Replace admin@example.com / YOUR_PASSWORD with your ADMIN_EMAIL / ADMIN_PASSWORD.

@base = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Wrong password -> 401 "Incorrect email or password."
POST {{base}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "admin@example.com", "password": "wrong-password"}

### 2. Login -> 200, returns a token (saved automatically as {{token}})
POST {{base}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "admin@example.com", "password": "YOUR_PASSWORD"}

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.token); %}

### 3. No token -> 401 "Please sign in."
GET {{base}}/api/products

### 4. Create category -> 201, id 1
POST {{base}}/api/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Electronics", "description": "Gadgets"}

### 5. Duplicate category (different capitals) -> 409
POST {{base}}/api/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "electronics"}

### 6. Create product with plenty of stock -> 201, id 1, status IN
POST {{base}}/api/products
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Keyboard", "sku": "kb-1", "categoryId": 1, "price": 1500, "stockQuantity": 10, "reorderThreshold": 5}

### 7. Create product that starts LOW -> 201, id 2, status LOW (an alert is created)
POST {{base}}/api/products
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Mouse", "sku": "MS-1", "categoryId": 1, "price": 600, "stockQuantity": 3, "reorderThreshold": 5}

### 8. Duplicate SKU (any letter case) -> 409 "This SKU is already used by another product."
POST {{base}}/api/products
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Other", "sku": "KB-1", "categoryId": 1, "price": 100, "stockQuantity": 1, "reorderThreshold": 1}

### 9. Invalid data -> 400 with fieldErrors (name, price)
POST {{base}}/api/products
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "", "sku": "X-1", "categoryId": 1, "price": 0, "stockQuantity": 1, "reorderThreshold": 1}

### 10. Filter low stock -> only "Mouse"
GET {{base}}/api/products?status=LOW
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 11. Active alerts -> exactly 1 (Mouse, LOW)
GET {{base}}/api/alerts?active=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 12. Add 20 to Mouse -> 201, stock 3 -> 23
POST {{base}}/api/inventory/products/2/adjust
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"type": "IN", "quantity": 20, "reason": "Restock received"}

### 13. Alert is now resolved: active list empty, resolved list has 1
GET {{base}}/api/alerts?active=false
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 14. Remove more than exists -> 409, stock unchanged
POST {{base}}/api/inventory/products/1/adjust
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"type": "OUT", "quantity": 50, "reason": "Lost"}

### 15. Create order (Idempotency-Key sent) -> 201, total 3000.00, Keyboard stock 10 -> 8
POST {{base}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: test-key-1
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerName": "Test Customer", "items": [{"productId": 1, "quantity": 2}]}

### 16. Send the SAME request again -> same order returned, NOT a second order (stock stays 8)
POST {{base}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: test-key-1
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerName": "Test Customer", "items": [{"productId": 1, "quantity": 2}]}

### 17. Too many items -> 409 "Not enough stock: Keyboard (only 8 left)."
POST {{base}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerName": "Test Customer", "items": [{"productId": 1, "quantity": 1000}]}

### 18. Only one order exists so far
GET {{base}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 19. Skip a step (PENDING -> DELIVERED) -> 409
PUT {{base}}/api/orders/1/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"status": "DELIVERED"}

### 20. Confirm -> 200
PUT {{base}}/api/orders/1/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"status": "CONFIRMED"}

### 21. Cancel -> 200, stock returned (Keyboard back to 10)
PUT {{base}}/api/orders/1/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"status": "CANCELLED"}

### 22. Keyboard stock is 10 again
GET {{base}}/api/products/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 23. Movement history shows the restock, the order deduction ("Order ORD-1001") and the cancel return
GET {{base}}/api/inventory/movements
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 24. Dashboard summary -> counts match what you did
GET {{base}}/api/dashboard/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 25. Create a STAFF user -> 201
POST {{base}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"fullName": "Staff Tester", "email": "staff@example.com", "password": "StaffPass123", "role": "STAFF"}

### 26. Login as staff (token saved as {{staffToken}})
POST {{base}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "staff@example.com", "password": "StaffPass123"}

> {% client.global.set("staffToken", response.body.token); %}

### 27. Staff can read -> 200
GET {{base}}/api/products
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### 28. Staff cannot delete -> 403 "You don't have permission to do that."
DELETE {{base}}/api/products/2
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### 29. Staff cannot manage users -> 403
GET {{base}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### 30. Admin can delete a product with no orders -> 204 (use product 2; product 1 is on an order so it would give 409)
DELETE {{base}}/api/products/2
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
